{"summary": "{
  "enabled_research": "The dataset uniquely permitted large-scale analysis of immune cell subsets in patients with ICI myocarditis, enabling the discovery of a unique population of cytotoxic CD8+ T cells re-expressing CD45RA (Temra) associated specifically with ICI myocarditis.",
  "practical_use": "Suitable for benchmarking and fine-tuning machine learning models for immune cell subset classification and biomarker discovery in cardiovascular diseases.",
  "why_useful": "The dataset is valuable due to its comprehensive human immune phenotyping data, including single-cell RNA sequencing, single-cell T-cell receptor sequencing, and time-of-flight mass cytometry, which allows for high-resolution immune profiling of myocarditis.",
  "requirements_or_setup": "Requires access to the Stanford FluPrint Database and institutional review board approval for patient recruitment and data collection.",
  "strengths_shown": "The dataset has been shown to enable accurate diagnosis and identification of biomarkers for ICI myocarditis, as well as provide insights into the molecular characteristics of circulating immune cell subsets.",
  "limitations_found": "The study notes that the sample size is limited, with only 52 patients analyzed using CyTOF and 30 patients analyzed using scRNA-seq. Additionally, the dataset may not be representative of all patient populations or disease states.",
  "usage_quotes": [
    "This ability to distinguish between individual cell states is particularly important for conditions that affect immune cell subtypes at a broad level such as in immune checkpoint inhibition.",
    "Deep immunophenotyping with single-cell RNA sequencing, single-cell T-cell receptor sequencing, and time-of-flight mass cytometry can be applied to biobanked patient populations such as that used in this study to gain detailed understanding of immune cell subsets in cardiac and other types of systemic inflammatory disorders.",
    "We present the first comprehensive cellular and transcriptomic profiling of the peripheral blood mononuclear cells of patients with recently diagnosed ICI myocarditis and control subjects using CyTOF, scRNA-seq, and single-cell TCR-seq."
  ]
}", "dataset_name": "The FluPRINT database", "source_length": 12800, "full_source_length": 76710, "num_context_blocks": 0, "extraction_strategy": "keyword"}

